From 74f111b11c45856e8d94237f78534543d30d9356 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:49:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 29/31] AROS: one flag set for the resident engine

On AROS every program runs on the one V8 in v8.library, so v8_flags is
shared by all of them.  V8 freezes flags after initialization by making
them read-only, but AROS mprotect does nothing, so a program started
later silently rewrote the flags under the ones already running:
Chromium's --minor-ms switched a running Node's heap to the paged
young generation and Node crashed in StartSweepNewSpace.

Once frozen, a flag now refuses a new value (reported through
v8.library) instead of being trapped, and the resident engine always
freezes even when an embedder asks it not to.  Cap wasm memories at
2048 pages by default: AROS backs a whole reservation with memory, so
this is the engine's limit for every embedder rather than a flag one
of them sets.  The GC's core counts are read per collection, since
programs sharing the engine have different platforms.
